<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Susquehannock</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Conestoga, Minquas, Andaste</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Susquehannock, also known as the Conestoga, Minquas and Andaste, were an Iroquoian people of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susquehanna-river">Susquehanna River</a> in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>, whose name means 'people of the muddy river'. First described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-smith-explorer">John Smith</a> in 1608, they traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and New Netherland, and made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a> in 1652, while suffering intermittent attacks by the Haudenosaunee. By the 1670s disease and war had sharply reduced them; in 1675 militias from Maryland and Virginia besieged their fort on Piscataway <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, and the survivors scattered, many joining the Haudenosaunee. The last community, at Conestoga Town, was massacred by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paxton-boys">Paxton Boys</a> in 1763.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…the Covenant Chain, the alliance made at Albany in 1677 with Governor Edmund Andros of New York and later extended to other colonies, they became the principal Native partner of the English and claimed authority over many dependent peoples, including the Delaware and remnant groups of the <b>Susquehannock</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Iroquois Confederacy · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>…moved whole peoples into the League: during the Beaver Wars the Haudenosaunee defeated and assimilated most of the Wendat (1649), Petun (1650), the Neutral Nation (1651), the Erie (1657) and the <b>Susquehannock</b> (1680), and in 1722 the Tuscarora, sponsored by the Oneida, were accepted as a sixth nation.</blockquote><a href="/societies/haudenosaunee">Social Hierarchy of the Haudenosaunee</a></li></ul></section>
